# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# Lines are chosen to be structurally distinct from their siblings. Codemark
# refuses a bookmark whose generated query matches more than one node, so a
# statement with an identically-shaped sibling is not a usable anchor (the
# Scala profile hit exactly this).

# Inside a conditional inside a method inside an inherent impl:
# impl LineItem > fn taxed > if self.taxable.
# The shallowest method chain, and `return` is the only one in that body.
78

# Inside a loop inside a conditional inside a method:
# impl Invoice > fn compute > for line > if line.amount == 0.0.
# The deepest control-flow chain; `continue` is the only one in the file.
122

# Inside a closure inside a method: impl Invoice > fn discounted > |amount|.
# Proves a closure_expression body is reachable — the landmark no sample can
# propose, since a Rust closure never wraps a declaration.
138

# Inside a method in an impl in a module: mod audit > impl Entry > fn record.
# Proves `module` and `impl` stack as containers.
176

# The deepest named chain: a function nested in a method, in an impl, in a
# module — mod audit > impl Entry > fn normalized > fn clamp. This is the line
# that proves a nested `function` lands in the trail.
185
